From fbdceb633aa22d8e16e44d951de6a99aea7c419c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:53:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel interfaces: execution policies

The options of the execution (`mfront_gpb_ExecutionOptions`,
`mfront_gpmp_ExecutionOptions`: `void* queue`, statistics, stack size) are
replaced by execution policies, one C++ class per backend, and by a
separate member for the statistics.

- `MFront/GenericParallel/`, namespace `mfront::generic_parallel`:
  `AbstractBackendExecutionPolicy` (virtual `getIdentifier`, declared before
  the virtual destructor so that its entry in the table of virtual functions
  is the same with the ABIs of Visual Studio and of MinGW), defined by the
  new `MFrontGenericParallelRuntime` library; `BackendExecutionCommonPolicy`
  (`preserve_stack_size`, `asynchronous`); `BackendExecutionPolicyBase`;
  one header per backend with a `make...` function: `cuda` and `hip`
  (stream), `sycl` (queue, required, identifier including the
  implementation of SYCL), `kokkos` (class template on the execution space),
  `raja` (class template on the resource of camp), `stlpar`, `openmp` and
  `openacc` (common options only); `BackendExecutionPolicy.h`, opaque type
  of the policies in C.
- `mfront_gpb_BatchData`, `mfront_gpb_RotationData` and
  `mfront_gpmp_BatchData`: `statistics`, then `execution_policy`; versions
  of the data structures 4.
- Rules of the generated functions, for behaviours, models and material
  properties: a null policy selects the default policy of the backend (none
  for `sycl`); a policy of another backend, or an asynchronous computation
  without statistics, are invalid arguments; given statistics defer the
  report, whether the computation is asynchronous or not; the generated
  function copies what it needs from the policy.
- Each library exports the identifier of the policy it expects
  (`<name>_generic_parallel_execution_policy`).
- `tfel-config --mfront-generic-parallel-runtime`.
- Tests: the comparisons and the tests of the material properties create the
  policy of the tested backend from the exported identifier, and check a
  policy of another backend, an asynchronous computation without statistics
  and a synchronous computation with statistics (all the functions,
  rotations included).
- Documentation of the interfaces and release notes.
